        "id": "s6",
        "kind": "your-turn",
        "title": "Your turn: the perpendicular bisector",
        "body": "The perpendicular bisector of $AB$ cuts $AB$ in half at right angles. It passes through the **midpoint** with the **perpendicular gradient**. For $A(2, 3)$ and $B(6, 7)$: midpoint $(4, 5)$, gradient of $AB$ is $1$, so the bisector has gradient $-1$ and equation $y = -x + 9$.",
