            "alt": "Triangle P(1, 1), Q(4, 7), R(7, minus 2) with the right angle at P where the gradients 2 and minus a half meet"
          },
          {
            "type": "worked-example",
            "problem": "$A(1, 1)$, $B(4, 3)$ and $C(2, 6)$. Show that angle $ABC$ is a right angle.",
            "steps": [
              {
                "text": "Gradient of $AB = \\dfrac{3 - 1}{4 - 1} = \\dfrac{2}{3}$"
              },
              {
                "text": "Gradient of $BC = \\dfrac{6 - 3}{2 - 4} = -\\dfrac{3}{2}$"
              },
              {
                "text": "$\\dfrac{2}{3} \\times \\left(-\\dfrac{3}{2}\\right) = -1$, so $AB$ is perpendicular to $BC$ and angle $ABC = 90°$"
              }
            ]
          }
